{"title":"2007 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">2007 CEMC Pascal #5</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2007 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">2007 CEMC Cayley #4</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The table shows the pay Leona earned for two different shifts at the same fixed hourly rate. How much will she earn for a five hour shift at this rate?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/1/951bbdac7c7b02c923d5b9d7a94ed53fbd4c99e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\$43.75 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\$46.25 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\$38.75 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\$36.25 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\$41.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"595\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the hourly rate is fixed, we can represent this as a linear function. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/3/5732d400ae37482541578ac7b7e64b73851b8ee8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(h)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" /> be the total pay at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> hours. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/015afed60af81a747baee7727dc81cffbe50a7da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(h) = mh + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is the rate and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the y-intercept\n</p><p>Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8d3aa5ffdecda42a087575d9dc32cc5553f3fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"104\" height=\"40\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/6208e251a68d320f6f92a0e9b71181925ecd49ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\frac{49.50 - 24.75}{6 - 3} = \\frac{24.75}{3} = \\$8.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"286\" height=\"40\" /> per hour\n</p><p>This means:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f6009a901b15fe1f6dd9bdd379f99e29f814d96e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(h) = 8.25h + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We can now plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b1af1c7c5d4066da1885524ca89c83dd263ccef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a4907759b24c0b2f887e9d2a9860607fec05aa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(h) = 8.25 \\times 3 + b = 24.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"219\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/c/d8c5fa3f446b37f8402bfb20929de1d20a44c821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24.75 + b = 24.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/8/c98954bfeb7f3569d05bec6ce089b391f7dfd856.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/968aacd9a71a20136a5ccda7c17649ed109219c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(h) = 8.25h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/e/55e796133f3ed1f652f3d1a51c418f19d5efb5cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05da62d750e44cafda16153285a2d8c1226c1e59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(5) = 8.25 \\times 5 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } \\$41.25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"242\" height=\"31\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1\">Solution 1.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can just simply subtract the slope from the amount at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours to find the amount of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours because exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hour passed.\n</p><p>Doing this, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9da14bc2603eda9c16c6f59fc27b1689e6cd591.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49.50 - 8.25 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } \\$41.25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"218\" height=\"31\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.2\">Solution 1.2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like solution 1.1, we can find the slope. However, we can add the slope twice to the amount at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours passed.\n</p><p>Doing this, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af30445e9aad550080ae8743339427d741723262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24.75 + 8.25 \\times 2 = 24.75 + 16.50 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } \\$41.25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"378\" height=\"31\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal\">2007 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2007 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title